 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "monsters is a list of rows [label, cost, defeats]. A label is the monster name, followed by \"*\" when the monster is hostile. The rows describe a tree rooted at root: every child name has its own row and appears in exactly one defeat list, and every row is reachable from root. Defeat is transitive: a monster can defeat exactly its strict descendants. Choose a set of non-hostile monsters such that every hostile monster is a strict descendant of at least one chosen monster. Return the minimum total cost (0 when there is no hostile monster), or -1 when some hostile monster has no non-hostile strict ancestor.",
  "provenance": [
